      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T19:14:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, that\u0027s probably an issue only on unit tests. In real code this is called through InboundSmsHandler which is itself a handler so has a looper associated with it, and you don\u0027t need to do anything, as in not even call super(). Unit tests on the other hand do not have a looper associated with them I believe, so in several tests we create a separate HandlerThread. See GsmCdmaPhoneTest.java for example that has a GsmCdmaPhoneTestHandler.\n\nSeparately, do make sure (maybe from logcat), that both this handler and the onFilterCallback are called on the same thread.",
